    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23316" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infrūnītus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		2. in-fruniscor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>unfit for enjoyment</i>, <i>tasteless</i>, <i>senseless</i>, <i>silly</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Vit. Beat. 13, 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mulier,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Ben. 3, 16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">copia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 5, 1 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Eccli. 31, 23</span></i>, and 23,
			6.— Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infrūnītē</span></b> , <i>senselessly</i> (late Lat.), Hilar. in Job, 3, p. 220.</div>
